        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. If your husband has left the UAE and is refusing to cooperate with divorce proceedings, you can file for judicial divorce (faskh) at the UAE Personal Status Court. For Muslim women: if he has been absent for 1 year or more without maintenance, Article 79 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024 provides an absence-based divorce. For non-Muslim women: the civil no-fault dissolution under Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2022 does not require the husband\'s cooperation at all, you file, the court waits 90 days, and the divorce is granted.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How long does absence divorce take in UAE?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'An absence-based judicial divorce under Article 79 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024 takes approximately 6-18 months from filing. The investigation period is 30-90 days, followed by a public notice period (typically 30-60 days), then a court hearing and judgment. If the husband appears or responds during this period, the timeline extends. Non-Muslim civil no-fault dissolution is faster: approximately 3-6 months from filing.',
      },
