    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What if I do not know where my husband is?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'If your husband\'s whereabouts are unknown, UAE courts can proceed by public notice. After the court makes reasonable attempts to locate the husband (including through last known address, email, WhatsApp, and relevant authorities), it publishes a notice in the official gazette and a widely-circulated Arabic newspaper. If the husband does not respond within the notice period, the court proceeds to judgment in his absence. You do not need to know his location to obtain a divorce in UAE.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I get maintenance while waiting for divorce?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. You can apply for an interim maintenance order at the Personal Status Court while divorce proceedings are pending. Courts can issue interim maintenance orders on an expedited basis, in urgent cases where you have no income and the husband has abandoned the family, courts can issue an order within 48-72 hours. The interim order covers your living expenses and any children\'s expenses until the divorce is finalised. The husband\'s non-presence does not prevent an interim order being issued.',
