        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'If the husband has been properly served (by all available means including email, WhatsApp, last known address, and if necessary publication in the gazette) and still does not respond, UAE courts proceed to judgment in absentia. His non-response is treated as a failure to contest the proceedings, not as a bar to the divorce being granted. Courts are experienced with absent respondents in divorce cases and have a clear procedural framework for proceeding without the husband.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Do I need a lawyer for absence divorce?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'You are not legally required to use a lawyer for absence divorce proceedings in UAE. However, given the complexity of serving process on an absent or foreign respondent, navigating the publication requirements, and presenting the financial abandonment evidence correctly, legal representation significantly increases the efficiency and success rate of the proceedings. Lawyer fees for an absence divorce case typically range from AED 5,000 to AED 25,000 depending on complexity.',
      },
