    question: 'Will I lose mahr rights by filing for absence divorce rather than waiting for talaq?',
    answer: "No. A judicial divorce (faskh) on grounds of absence or financial abandonment does not forfeit the wife's mahr rights. Unlike khula, where the wife typically returns the mahr as the price of the dissolution, a faskh is granted because of the husband's wrongdoing or incapacity. The wife retains full mahr rights. The deferred mahr falls due on the divorce judgment. If the husband has been absent and has no known UAE assets, enforcing the mahr may require international cooperation, but the legal right to the mahr is entirely preserved.",
